From: substrate
Subject: conf: default to master_process off on substrate

nginx's master/worker process model does not yet bring up a worker
on substrate: the master forks but the child never reaches its
accept() loop, so a stock master+worker config opens the listen
socket and then never answers a request (only the master shows in
ps; error.log stays empty).

Single-process mode (master_process off) works fully -- one process
manages and serves, daemonizes normally, and answers requests
(verified: GET / returns 200 with the default index over loopback).
Ship it as the default so a plain `nginx` works out of the box.

Revert once substrate's fork / process-channel path supports nginx
workers.

--- a/conf/nginx.conf
+++ b/conf/nginx.conf
@@ -2,6 +2,14 @@
 #user  nobody;
 worker_processes  1;
 
+# substrate: nginx's master/worker model does not yet spawn a worker
+# on substrate (the master forks but the child never reaches the
+# accept loop), so a default master+worker config listens but never
+# answers.  Run single-process instead: one process both manages and
+# serves.  It still daemonizes normally.  Remove this once substrate's
+# fork/process-channel path supports nginx workers.
+master_process off;
+
 #error_log  logs/error.log;
 #error_log  logs/error.log  notice;
 #error_log  logs/error.log  info;
